    {
      "issue": "Stabilized NOI does not agree across tabs",
      "detail": "The Summary and Scenarios tabs both carry [[noi_stab]], while the Property P&L computes [[noi_pl_y3]] in Year 3. The payback, cap rate and IRR stated in this memo derive from the Summary figure, which is the more conservative of the two. The P&L expense lines should be reconciled to the scenario model before this package goes to the lender."
    }
  ],
  "risks": [
    {
      "risk": "Lease-up runs slower than plan and stabilized occupancy arrives a year late.",
      "response": "The downside case already prices this: payback extends to [[down_pb]] months while coverage stays above covenant. A month-nine occupancy gate triggers a hold on rents rather than a discount."
    },
    {
      "risk": "The Year 2 reassessment lands above the modeled property tax line.",
      "response": "Taxes are the single largest expense line and are modeled at the assessor's published schedule. A reassessment materially above it would move NOI, and is the one variable worth a contingency reserve."
    },
    {
      "risk": "Construction overruns the approved budget.",
      "response": "Draw is staged against three milestones with a fixed-price general contract. No funds release before the guaranteed maximum price is executed."
    }
